# Cursor Rules: go-e Wallbox iOS App

## Project Overview
iOS app (SwiftUI, MVVM) for controlling a go-e Wallbox EV charger via local HTTP API.
See CONTEXT.md for API reference and business logic. See ARCHITECTURE.md for project structure.

---

## Workspace / Working Directory

- Always work in the local repository at `/Users/florianseichter/Projects/Go-E-Wallbox-Charging-App`
- Do not use Cursor worktrees unless explicitly requested by the user

---

## Code Style

- Swift 5.9+, SwiftUI, async/await – no Combine, no callbacks
- Use `@Observable` (iOS 17) – not `ObservableObject` unless explicitly told to target iOS 16
- Prefer `struct` over `class` for models
- No force unwraps (`!`) anywhere – use `guard let` or `if let`
- Explicit error handling – never use `try?` to silently swallow errors
- No hardcoded strings for UI text – use constants or localization keys
- No hardcoded IP addresses or numeric constants – all go through AppSettings

---

## Architecture Rules (non-negotiable)

- Views contain zero business logic – only layout and user interaction forwarding
- ViewModels contain zero URLSession or HTTP code – always call through WallboxService
- WallboxService is the only place that knows about the go-e API
- All user preferences (IP, battery size, target SOC, loss factor) go through AppSettings
- Never bypass the ViewModel to call a Service directly from a View

---

## What You Must Never Do

- Do not install third-party packages without asking first
- Do not refactor files that are not relevant to the current task
- Do not change the project structure without being asked
- Do not add features beyond what is explicitly requested
- Do not use deprecated APIs
- Do not use DispatchQueue – use async/await instead
- Do not create new files without listing them first and confirming

---

## Error Handling

- All network calls must have explicit error states surfaced to the UI
- Use a consistent pattern: `isLoading: Bool`, `errorMessage: String?` in every ViewModel
- Never fail silently

---

## When You Are Unsure

- Ask before creating new files
- Ask before adding a dependency
- If the API response format is unclear, refer to CONTEXT.md first
- If a feature wasn't discussed, implement only the minimal version and flag it

---

## API Conventions

- All API calls go to `http://<ip>/api/` – base URL comes from AppSettings
- Preferred default wallbox IP: `192.168.178.69`
- Use `dwo` in Wh (multiply kWh × 1000) – never send kWh directly
- Always refresh status after a SET call to confirm the change was applied
- Polling interval: 15–20 seconds

---

## Commit Hygiene (reminders for the developer)

- Commit after every working feature – not after every file change
- If the agent breaks something, revert to last commit rather than trying to fix forward

---

## Git Branching (agent workflow)

- Never commit directly on `main` unless the user explicitly asks for it
- New work always starts from an up-to-date `main` (or the user’s chosen base branch) on a dedicated branch:
  - Features: `feature/<short-kebab-description>` (no ticket numbers; describe the outcome, e.g. `feature/live-wallbox-status`)
  - Bug fixes: `bugfix/<short-kebab-description>`
- Avoid Cursor-generated branch names like `cursor/<id>`; prefer the naming scheme above
- When creating GitHub pull requests (via MCP or otherwise), create **normal** pull requests by default (**not** drafts). Only use draft PRs if the user explicitly asks for a draft.
